WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.297
Before changing the messy dataset, we measure its problems.

00:00:04.297 --> 00:00:09.497
The example checks missing values, duplicate rows, and data types.

00:00:09.497 --> 00:00:14.267
This gives us a baseline and helps us document what needs attention.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:18.272
The is N A function identifies missing values.

00:00:18.272 --> 00:00:25.692
The duplicated function checks repeated rows, and the data types output shows how each column is stored.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:33.882
These checks are simple, but they are extremely useful because they turn vague impressions into measurable issues.

00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:42.837
A strong cleaning workflow follows a simple principle: measure first, change second, and verify afterward.

00:00:42.837 --> 00:00:47.486
That makes your process easier to explain and easier to debug.
